The reason I said that is because I tried to code a solution without Regex, replacing with .split and loops, but thought was too much work and gave up :P
My solution is basically 50% Regex hahah
Also, the -y flag is so trick @-@ the first thing I did was remove vowels from the input line, but that would remove the vowels in --title and --keywords too, so I cooked an spaghetti code for this problem.

readline();
let line = readline();
let y = line.includes("-y");
let title = line.match(/(?:-t|--title) (\S+)/)?.[1];
let kws = line.match(/--keyword((?: \w+)+)/)?.[1].split(/\s+/g) ?? [];
let out = [kws.map(kw => `[${kw}]`).join(" "), title].join(" ");
if (y) out = out.replace(/[aeiou]/ig, "");
print(out.replaceAll("[]", "").split(/\s+/).join(" ").trim() || "<BLANK>");
